{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1319,
    "dDurationMs": 4741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine a future cat-topia where both cats\nand people are applying to the physics and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6060,
    "dDurationMs": 1299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "astronomy departments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7359,
    "dDurationMs": 4471,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In astronomy, 2 cats are accepted and 2 are\nrejected, while 1 human is accepted and 1"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11830,
    "dDurationMs": 1299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is rejected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13129,
    "dDurationMs": 4341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In physics 1 cat gets in and 2 don't, while\n2 humans get in 4 don't."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17470,
    "dDurationMs": 5190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, overall at the university, 3 cats are\naccepted and 4 rejected for a 43% acceptance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22660,
    "dDurationMs": 5090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rate, while 3 humans are accepted and 5 rejected\nfor a 38% acceptance rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27750,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is the university discriminating against humans\nin its application process?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31900,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Possibly not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32900,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because if each department reviews\nits own applications, then the numbers show"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36620,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the astronomy department lets in 50%\nof cats and 50% of humans, which seems fair,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41280,
    "dDurationMs": 4930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the physics department lets in 33% of\ncats and 33% of humans, which again seems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46210,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fair."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47210,
    "dDurationMs": 3779,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The reason, then, for the apparent unfairness\nat the university level is the imbalance in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50989,
    "dDurationMs": 4601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how many cats and humans apply to each department:\nmore of the cats applied to the astronomy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55590,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "department, which happened to let in more\napplicants (regardless of species), while"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59820,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more of the humans applied to physics, which\nlet in fewer applicants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63690,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This situation is another illustration of\nSimpson's statistical paradox, and something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68490,
    "dDurationMs": 4730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like it actually happened at Berkeley in the\n1970s, which realized it was letting in 44%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73220,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of men applying to the graduate school, but\nonly 35% of women."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77640,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Careful analysis was able to show that women\ntended to apply more to departments that had"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81420,
    "dDurationMs": 5129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less funding and fewer places, like English,\nand men tended to apply more to less competitive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86549,
    "dDurationMs": 1691,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "departments, like engineering."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88240,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus within each department (which was the\nlevel at which applications were evaluated),"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92130,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there wasn’t obvious evidence of gender\ndiscrimination among applicants – if anything,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96100,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "women were favored."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97420,
    "dDurationMs": 4199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet, the unequal distribution of women\nand men across departments resulted in an"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101619,
    "dDurationMs": 3311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unequal distribution of women and men at the\nuniversity overall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104930,
    "dDurationMs": 4469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The question, then, is what caused the unequal\ndistribution of women and men to begin with?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109399,
    "dDurationMs": 4921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One can of course imagine a sinister institution\nknowing how Simpson's paradox works, wanting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114320,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to discriminate against a particular group,\nand thus advertising smaller, more competitive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118450,
    "dDurationMs": 4029,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "departments more heavily to that group, and\nvice-versa for groups they want to promote"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122479,
    "dDurationMs": 4841,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": ". More realistically, certain departments\nor fields may have reputations for being unwelcoming"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127320,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and unsupportive towards women even if they\nlet them in fairly, and it’s also possible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131220,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that aspects of a university itself attract\napplicants who are more likely to follow gendered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136000,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "career stereotypes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137720,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But ultimately, as the Berkeley study concluded,\nthe problem is a bigger, societal, one: “Women"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141400,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are shunted towards fields of study that are\ngenerally more crowded, less productive of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142400,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "completed degrees, less well funded, and that\nfrequently offer poorer professional employment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143400,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prospects…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144400,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The absence of a demonstrable bias in the\nadmissions system does not give grounds for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146500,
    "dDurationMs": 12250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "concluding that there must be no bias anywhere\nelse in the educational "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158750,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "process.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159750,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those words were written in a statistics paper\nin 1975."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163390,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And more recent statistics tell us that they\nstill remain true today - which is unfortunate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167330,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you think women and men should have equal\nopportunities and/or be paid equally for equal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171530,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172530,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the paradox isn’t really in the statistics,\nsince after careful analysis, the statistics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176470,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tell us we’re biased and even hint at where\nthose biases are (or aren’t) coming into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180590,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "play."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181590,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, the paradox is that we’ve remained so\nreluctant to fight our biases, even when they’re"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186310,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "put in plain sight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190080,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video is sponsored by Skillshare, the\nonline learning site with courses on all sorts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194620,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of creative, business and technology skills\n– like proper knife skills, or how to make"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199330,
    "dDurationMs": 4870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "animated graphs for a video, or how to fly\na drone, or how to design a logo for your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204200,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "knife-carrying drone-flying animated-graph\ncompany, and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207830,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can get two months free by going to skl.sh/MinutePhysics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211350,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, that’s skl.sh/MinutePhysics"
    } ]
  } ]
}
